            <ArticleTitle>Risk management in clinical practice. Part 8. Temporomandibular disorders.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>433-49</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1038/sj.bdj.2010.981</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Temporomandibular disorders can arise apparently idiopathically, as a result of macro-trauma or micro-trauma such as parafunction, as a result of a separate disease process or as a consequence of dental treatment. The objectives of this chapter are to make the practitioner aware of his/her responsibilities in any of these situations. Precise record keeping and careful risk management are essential. Guidelines are given to protect not only the practitioner but also the patient.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
